      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s first sentence (“Self-definition is the way a person understands and describes who they are as part of their self-concept”) is not supported by the provided packet text, which discusses “self-concept” levels (individual, relational, collective) rather than defining self-definition as a general process of understanding/describing oneself.",
        "The definition’s second sentence (“In this packet, it specifically refers to defining oneself through group membership, as in a collective self-concept”) is only partially supported: the packet states that collective self-concept “involves a self-definition based on group membership,” but it does not establish that “self-definition” in the packet is specifically limited to that meaning beyond this context."
